  note    Go's File.Sync and Python's os.fsync on a folder opened to read do it on POSIX, and Rust's File::sync_all where the folder can be opened, each in the stream's block; Darwin's F_FULLFSYNC is asked first, as io.sync asks it of a file. Windows has no call a page promises it of a folder: `unsupported` there, where write_atomic's rename is written through instead

